/*Q15. You are developing a Library Fine Calculation System using Java classes, constructors, and methods.
Create a static nested class named Library inside the provided LibraryFinCalculator class. The Library class must contain the following
instance variables:
• String bookId — represents the book ID.
• String title — represents the book title.
• int borrowedDays — represents the number of days the book was borrowed.
• double finePerDay — represents the fine charged per late day.
Constructor
Create a constructor Library(String bookld, String title, int borrowedDays, double finePerDay) to initialize all four instance variables.
Method
Implement calculateFine(int allowedDays) in the Library class.
The method should:
• Calculate the fine if borrowedDays is greater than allowedDays.
• Use the formula:
fine = (borrowedDays - allowedDays) x finePerDay
• Display the calculated fine rounded to 2 decimal places.
• Display "No Fine" if the book was returned within the allowed number of days.
The LibraryFinCalculator class should read the book details and allowed days, create a Library object, and call calculateFine().
Input Format:
• The first line contains a string representing the book id.
• The second line contains a string representing the book title.
• The third line contains an integer representing the number of days the book was borrowed.
• The fourth line contains a floating-point number representing the fine per day in rupees.
• The fifth line contains an integer representing the number of allowed days.
Output Format:
• Print the output of calculateFine(allowedDays).

*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class LibraryFinCalculator {
 
    static class Library {
        String bookId;
        String title;
        int borrowedDays;
        double finePerDay;
 
        Library(String bookId, String title, int borrowedDays, double finePerDay) {
            this.bookId = bookId;
            this.title = title;
            this.borrowedDays = borrowedDays;
            this.finePerDay = finePerDay;
        }
 
        void calculateFine(int allowedDays) {
            if (borrowedDays > allowedDays) {
                double fine = (borrowedDays - allowedDays) * finePerDay;
                System.out.printf("%.2f%n", fine);
            } else {
                System.out.println("No Fine");
            }
        }
    }
 
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String id = sc.nextLine().trim();
        String title = sc.nextLine().trim();
        int borrowed = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
        double fine = Double.parseDouble(sc.nextLine().trim());
        int allowed = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
        Library lib = new Library(id, title, borrowed, fine);
        lib.calculateFine(allowed);
        sc.close();
    }
}
